hedule and suggestor outcomes\n\nAddresses three review findings on this PR, each checked against the code first:\n- the wizard_module fixture opened 'dashboard/pages/3_Scenario_Wizard.py' relative to the working directory\n  (8 errors when pytest ran from another directory); it now resolves from Path(__file__).\n- the schedule test only asserted that SOME 'Interpolated k' metric existed. It now asserts every margin\n  computation uses the schedule model with the loaded schedule, the term and reference sigma of the last one,\n  the metric values (k = margin / (reference_sigma * total capital) = 0.50, margin $5.0M) and that the table\n  shown IS the loaded schedule.\n- the suggestions=None case only asserted the absence of a warning. It now asserts positive evidence that the\n  renderer ran through its inputs (the last widget before the button stored its value) and stored no suggestions.\nNot changed: the finding that a patched 'st' leaks between cases. The fixture builds a fresh namespace per test\n(runpy.run_path), so nothing leaks.\n\nBreak-and-revert on the page: doubling k, showing a different table, a wrong term in the last margin call and an\nearly return in the suggestor are each caught by these tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-10-16T22:43:11Z","author":{"name":"stranske","email":"stranske@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com"}},"repository":{"id":996036804,"node_id":"R_kgDOO15QxA","name":"Portable-Alpha-Extension-Model","full_name":"stranske/Portable-Alpha-Extension-Model","private":false,"owner":{"login":"stranske","id":23046322,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDQ2MzIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23046322?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske","html_url":"https://github.com/stranske","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stranske/followers","foll